$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Phenacyl-1H-benzimidazole
3-Chlorophenylhydrazone (1c). A mixture of 2-phenacyl-1H-benzimidazole
(10 mmol), 3-chlorophenylhydrazine hydrochloride (11 mmol), pyridine (15
mmol), and dioxane (5 ml) was heated at 95-100°C for 1.5 h. We added
water (3 ml) and 2-propanol (3 ml) and stirred the mixture until
crystallization began. After cooling the precipitate was filtered off,
washed with 2-propanol, and dried at 115°C for 5 h under the vacuum of a
water-jet pump. Yield: 77%, pure. Empirical formula: C21H17ClN4, Found,
%: C 69.78, H 4.63, N 15.47, Calculated, %: C 69.90, H 4.75, N 15.53, mp:
225-226.5 °C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1, C═N, C═O and N-H: 1595, 3365, 1H NMR
spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 4.45 (2H, s, CH2); 6.83 (1H, d, J = 8.1,
3-ClC6H4: H-4); 7.08-7.17 (2H, m, H-5,6); 7.20-7.26 (1H, m, p-protons
C6H5); 7.26-7.31 (3H, m, 3-ClC6H4: H-2,4,5); 7.35-7.40 (2H, m, m-protons
C6H5); 7.45 (1H, d, J = 6.9, H-7); 7.52 (1H, d, J = 7.2, H-4); 7.85 (2H,
d, J = 7.5, o-protons C6H5); 10.39 (1H, s, NNH); 12.40 (1H, s, H-1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isomerization of 2-phenacyl-1H-benzimidazole arylhydrazones to
1-aryl-5-(o-aminoanilino)-3-phenylpyrazoles by trifluoroacetylation and
hydrazinolysis
