$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Phenacyl-1H-benzimidazole 4-Tolylhydrazone (1e). A mixture of
2-phenacyl-1H-benzimidazole (5 mmol), 4-tolylhydrazine (7 mmol), and
dioxane (5 ml) was heated for 1.5 h in the presence of five drops of
glacial acetic acid at 95-100°C. We added water (2.5 ml) and stirred the
mixture until crystallization began. After cooling the precipitate was
filtered off, washed with 2-propanol, and dried at 115°C for 5 h under
the vacuum of a water-jet pump. Yield: 75%, pure. Empirical formula:
C22H20N4, Found, %: C 77.68, H 5.82, N 16.32, Calculated, %: C 77.62, H
5.92, N 16.46, mp: 221-222.5 °C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1, C═N, C═O and N-H:
1610, 3340, 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 2.24 (3H, s, CH 3); 4.41
(2H, s, CH2); 7.08-7.18 (2 × 2H, 2d, J = 8.4, 4-CH3 C6H4); 7.09-7.16 (2H,
m, H-5,6); 7.23-7.28 (1H, m, p-protons C6H5); 7.33-7.38 (2H, m, m-protons
C6H5); 7.44 (1H, d, J = 6.9, H-7); 7.52 (1H, d, J = 7.2, H-4); 7.84 (2H,
d, J = 7.8, o-protons C6H5); 10.20 (1H, s, NNH); 12.40 (1H, s, H-1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isomerization of 2-phenacyl-1H-benzimidazole arylhydrazones to
1-aryl-5-(o-aminoanilino)-3-phenylpyrazoles by trifluoroacetylation and
hydrazinolysis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dzvinchuk, I. B.; Lozinskii, M. O.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Chemistry of Heterocyclic Compounds (New York, NY, United States) (2005),
41(7), 845-849

