(5) and the appropriate aldehyde in glacial acetic acid was refluxed for
3-4 hr. The reaction mixture was cooled, poured into crushed ice and the
deposited solid was collected, washed several times with cold water and
then crystallized from the proper solvent to give (7a-e) (Table II).
Compd. No. 7b, yield 72%. m.p. °C (solvent of cryst): 124 (pet.ether)
(100-120°C); Molecular formula: C22H20N4O4Se; IR: 1620 cm-1 (C=N), 1715
cm-1 (C=O), 1550n 1345 cm-1 (NO2), 1460 cm-1 (OCH3). 1H NMR (DMSO), δ 3.2
(d, 2H, CH2), δ 3.7 (s, 3H, CH3), δ 7.4-8.3 (m, 12H, Ar-H), δ 8.5 (s, 1H,
N=CH), δ 10.1 (s, 1H, NHCO) and δ 8.8 (B, 1H, NH)
