$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 10 mL anhydrous ethanol, 0.05 g furfuraldehyde
and 0.18 g compound 2 were dissolved in a 25 mL round-bottom flask. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 min, after that
large amounts of precipitate formed. The reaction was performed for
further 0.5 h. The insoluble substance was filtrated with suction, washed
with anhydrous ethanol and recrystallized from DMF-ethanol-H2O to give 3a
as an acicular crystal (0.20 g). 3e, 64 %, white solid m.p. 202-203 °C;
1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300 MHz) δ: 10.98 (s, 1H, NH), 9.87 (s, 1H, OH), 7.78
(s, 1H, CH=N), 6.73-7.41 (m, 7H, ArH), 3.31-4.09 (m, 16H, 4 × OCH2CH2O);
13C NMR δ: 159.3, 152.1, 147.9, 147.5, 130.5, 128.5, 124.7, 121.1, 115.6,
112.4, 111.7, 70.5, 69.6, 68.4; IR (KBr) ν: 3174 (NH), 1607 (N=C), 1275,
1046 (Ar-O-CH2), 1139 (CH2-O-CH2) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 466.2 (M+, 0.72),
438.3 (1.06), 368.4 (1.10), 332.0 (7.47), 315.1 (2.25), 300.0 (14.15),
268.1 (36.84), 182.9 (25.58), 167.9 (43.94), 136.0 (100), 120.9 (60.15),
105.9 (78.00), 77.9 (41.60), 76.9 (34.69). Anal. calcd for C21H26N2SO8: C
54.07, H 5.62, N 6.01; found C 54.23, H 5.68, N 6.21.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
