$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Hydrazination of 2H-chromene-2,4(3H)-diones 7 and 10 ( general procedure
). A solution of 3 mmol of compound 7 or 10 in 20 mL of propan-2-ol was
heated to the boiling point, 3 mmol of hydrazine hydrate was added, and
the mixture was heated for 24 h under reflux. The mixture was cooled, and
the precipitate was filtered off, washed with propan-2-ol, and dried.
3,5-Diphenyl-5,5a-dihydrochromeno[4,3-c][1,2]-diazepin-6(4H)-one (8).
Yield 60%, colorless crystals. mp 121-122°C (from i-PrOH). IR spectrum,
ν, cm-1: 1710 (C=O), 1680 (C=N), 1100 (C-O-C). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm:
2.68 d.d and 3.40 d.d (1H each, 2 J = 16, 3 J = 4 Hz), 4.30-4.50 m (1H,
CH), 4.98 d (1H, 5a-H, 3 J = 5 Hz), 6.78-8.08 m (14H, Harom). Found, %: C
77.67; H 4.95; N 7.25. C24H18N2O2. Calculated, %: C 77.67; H 4.95; N
7.65.
