$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Condensation of 2 with Free Sugars: Formation
of 17a-f and 18 General Procedure A mixture of 2 (2.74 g, 0.01 mol) and
aldohexoses, namely: D-glucose, D-galactose, D-mannose, aldopentoses,
namely: D-ribose, L-arabinose, D-xylose, and/or fructose (0.01 mol) was
refluxed in dioxane (20 ml) for 4 horns (TLC). After cooling, the
precipitated solid was filtered off, washed with ethanol and
recrystallized from DMF. 17a-f and 18.
4-Amino-6-[2-(4-methoxyphenyl)vinyl]-3-[N'-(2,3,4,5-tetrahydroxypentylidene)hydrazine]-4H-[1,2,4]triazin-5-one
(17e). Using L-arabinose in the general procedure gave 17e. (60%). m.p.
200-201°C; IR (KBr), 1597 (CN), 3319 (OH) cm-1; 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6) δ 2.78
(s, 3H, CH3O-4), 3.65-4.08 (m, 4H, OH), 4.35 (t, 1H, J = 6.85 Hz, H-4'),
4.62 (t, 1H, J = 5.27 Hz, H-3'), 4.82 (d, 1H, J =3.49 Hz, H-2'), 4.96 (d,
1H, J =5.99 Hz, H-1'), 5.19 (s, Η, NH), 5.51 (s, 2H, NH2), 6.74-7.45 (m,
6H, Harom), 7.68 (s, 1H, N = CH). Anal. For C17H22N6O6 Calcd.: C, 50.24;
H, 5.46; N, 20.68. Found: C, 50.23; H, 5.41; N, 20.44.
