$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-Hydroxy-3-(2-hydroxyaryl)-5-polyfluoroalkyl-Δ2-pyrazolines (3).
Chromanone 2 (1.3 mmol) was dissolved in a minimum volume of ethanol (2-3
mL) at ~20 °C, and 25% hydrazine hydrate (0.5 mL) was added. The solution
was left at ~20 °C;for 15 min and then diluted with water (10-15 mL). The
crystalline product that precipitated (sometimes it was oil, which is
gradually solidified) was filtered off, washed with water, dried, and
recrystallized from a hexane-toluene mixture (toluene with a butanol
additive was used for compound 3c). Compound 3k: Yield 57% M.p. 145-146
°C; C13H14F4N2O2; IR, v/cm-1 3360, 1635, 1585
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
