$DATUM Hydrazination of 3,3′-(arylmethylene)bis[2H-chromene-2,4(3H)-diones] 12a
and 15 ( general procedure ). Hydrazine hydrate, 0.2 g (4.90 mmol), was
added dropwise to a solution of 2.43 mmol of compound 12 or 15 in 12 mL
of a 3: 1 mixture of propan-2-ol and chloroform. The mixture was heated
for 24 h under reflux and cooled, and the precipitate was filtered off,
washed with propan-2-ol, and dried.
3,3′-(Phenylmethylene)bis(4-hydrazinyl-2H-chromen-2-one) (14). Yield 0.5
g (53%), orange crystals. mp 203-204°C (from i-PrOH). IR spectrum, ν,
cm-1: 3400-3300 (NH, NH2), 1750 (C=O), 1650 (C=C). 1H NMR spectrum, δ,
ppm: 3.64 s (1H, CH), 6.90-7.50 m (13H, Harom), 8.48 br.s (6H, NH, NH2).
Found, %: C 67.84; H 5.02; N 13.05. C25H20N4O4. Calculated, %: C 68.17; H
4.58; N 12.72.
