$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-Hydroxy-3-(2-hydroxyaryl)-1-phenyl-5-polyfluoroalkyl-Δ2-pyrazolines
(6). Chromanone 2 (1.15 mmol) was dissolved in 2-3 mL of ethanol at -20
°C, and a 4 M ethanolic solution (0.3 mL) of phenylhydrazine was added.
The solution was left at -20 °C for 1 week, then the solvent was
evaporated, and the residue was washed with 70% ethanol, dried, and
recrystallized from a hexane-toluene mixture. Compound 6m: Yield 46% M.p.
132-133 °C; C16H12ClF3N2O2; IR, v/cm-1 3410, 1600, 1560
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 2-Polyfluoroalkylchromones. 11. Synthesis and structures of
5-hydroxy-3-(2-hydroxyaryl)-5-polyfluoroalkyl-Δ2-pyrazolines and
3(5)-(2-hydroxyaryl)-5(3)-polyfluoroalkylpyrazoles
