$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Hydrazination of 1,5-diketones 1a and 1b (
general procedure ). A solution of 3 mmol of 1,5-diketone 1a or 1b in 30
mL of propan-2-ol was heated to 80°C, 12 mmol of hydrazine hydrate was
added, and the mixture was kept for 24 h. The precipitate was filtered
off and washed with water. Recrystallization from propan-2-ol gave
compound 2, and compound 3 was isolated by evaporation of the filtrate.
The oily material obtained in the reaction with 1b was treated with
diisopropyl ether, and subsequent recrystallization from propan-2-ol
afforded diazepine 4. 1-Phenyl-2-(3-phenyl-3,3a,4,5-tetrahydro-2H-benzo[
g]indazol-3-yl)ethanone (2). Yield 30%, colorless crystals.
5-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-3-phenyl-6,7-dihydro-4H-naphtho[ 1,2-c][1,2]diazepine
(4). Yield 22%, colorless crystals. mp 182-183°C (from i-PrOH). IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3055, 3037, 3026 (C-Harom), 2996-2834 (C-Haliph), 1669
(C=C), 1571-1510 (C=Carom), 1510-1491 (C=N). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm:
2.54-2.82 m (4H, CH2), 3.92 s (3H, OCH3), 4.00 d (2H, 4-H, J = 16 Hz),
6.94-7.64 m (13H, Harom). Found, %: C 82.30; H 6.42; N 7.46. C26H22N2O.
Calculated, %: C 82.51; H 5.86; N 7.40.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemistry of 1,5-diketones: V. Hydrazination of acyclic and heterocyclic
(poly)carbonyl compounds
